<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Title (210)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>title &lt;player&gt; &lt;title&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>title Herdas Master of the Under-dark
</pre>
<p>Sets a player's title, the words after their name in <a cmd='#'>who</a> and when 
others see them. The player, who can be anywhere in the game, is told 
"Your title changed.", and the change is logged with who made it.
</p><p>The guidelines for titles, from the old help:
</p>
<ul><li>keep it to one line, so that it doesn't wrap in who or in the room;</li>
<li>no tags of your own: the game adds those like Guide, Builder or Admin itself;</li>
<li>no special characters such as&#160;! @ # $&#160;% ^ &amp; * ( );</li>
<li>nothing vulgar or obscene, no curses, flames or anything out of the game's world;</li>
<li>in English.</li></ul>
<p>For example, "Herdas - Master of The Under-dark" is fine; "Herdas - Seeker 
of The Under-dark [Tag] * LORD *" is not. If a title may not be fitting, 
don't set it, and let the player choose another.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Title</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ctitle</a>
</pre>




</div>